e-linejoin=\"miter\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#087e83\" d=\"M430 550 325 517\"/>\n<path transform=\"matrix(1,0,0,-1,-104.1,717.9)\" d=\"M325 517 332.9155 515.8402 330.8289 522.4795Z\" fill=\"#087e83\" fill-rule=\"evenodd\"/>\n</g>\n</svg>\n","4 1 3 2 · 4 1 3 2 · 1 4 2 3 · 1 2 3 4"],["heading","HOW TO READ THE DIAGRAM"],["text","1. Merge sort splits the input into halves, sorts each half, then merges them."],["text","2. Quicksort instead selects a pivot; with pivot 3, partition [4,1,3,2] into [1,2], [3], [4]."],["text","3. Recursively sort the partitions. Both finish at [1,2,3,4]."],["heading","INTERVIEW MEMORY TIP"],["text","Merge sort has O(n log n) worst-case time; typical quicksort can degrade to O(n^2)."]]